// Introduction
// =====================================================================================================================
// Create your data link configuration in a static manner here, using x-macros.
// The example below indicates how to create such a configuration.
// Note that it is not necessary to nest the channels as shown, though it is recommended
// to follow this pattern so that you have an easier time. This implementation allows the
// configuration of 8 data link objects:
//
// - PHYSICAL_CHANNEL: Stores core data link parameters
// - MASTER_CHANNEL_TM: Main telemetry channel
// - MASTER_CHANNEL_TC: Main telecommand channel
// - VIRTUAL_CHANNEL_TM: Granularizes telemetry traffic of MASTER_CHANNEL_TM to multiple streams
// - VIRTUAL_CHANNEL_TC: Granularizes telecommand traffic of MASTER_CHANNEL_TC to multiple streams
// - MAP_CHANNEL: Granularizes telecommand traffic of a single VIRTUAL_CHANNEL_TC to multiple streams
// - COP1: A closed loop procedure that manages telecommand acknowledgement
// - SECURITY_ASSOCIATION: Offers frame encryption and authentication services to traffic in VIRTUAL_CHANNEL_TC
//                         and MAP_CHANNEL.
//
// General rules:
// =====================================================================================================================
// - Define one PHYSICAL_CHANNEL() per link
// - Define one MASTER_CHANNEL_TM() per PHYSICAL_CHANNEL()
// - Define at least one VIRTUAL_CHANNEL_TM() per MASTER_CHANNEL_TM()
// - Define at least one VIRTUAL_CHANNEL_TC() per MASTER_CHANNEL_TC()
// - Definition of MAP_CHANNEL() is optional. Note however, that if a VIRTUAL_CHANNEL_TC()
//   has at least one MAP_CHANNEL(), then frames cannot be inserted directly to the VIRTUAL_CHANNEL_TC()
//   itself, but rather on one of it's MAP_CHANNELS
// - TM channels should be associated with TM channels only. Same for TC.
// - Channels that have the same id and name, but different types of frames (TM/TC) are allowed
// - If there exists at least one defined TC channel with enabled COP, it is necessary that at least
//   one TM channel with an operational control field is also defined. This guarantees that
//   a return path for TC frame acknowledgements is available
//
// Configuration Parameters:
// =====================================================================================================================
// - PHYSICAL_CHANNEL(physicalChannelName,
//                    pcid,
//                    tfvn,
//                    maxTcLength,
//                    tmLength,
//                    maxFramesPdu,
//                    maxPduLength,
//                    bitRate,
//                    fecPresent)
//   -- physicalChannelName: A name that can be used to uniquely identify this physical channel
//   -- pcid: An 8 bit id to uniquely identify this physical channel. It is not part of the CCSDS standards, and is not
//            carried by any frame. It is added for addressing consistency with the other channels
//   -- tfvn: Transfer frame version number. Enter the value: "TransferFrameVersionNumber::TM_TC_SYNCHRONOUS_TRANSFER_FRAME_V1"
//   -- maxTcLength: The maximum allowed length of a TC frame (in bytes)
//   -- tmLength: The length of the TM frame in bytes
//   -- maxFramesPdu: TODO implement?
//   -- maxPduLength: TODO implement?
//   -- bitRate: The bitrate of the link, in bits per second TODO no use for this yet
//   -- fecPresent: A non zero number indicates that frames on this physical channel will have a frame error
//                  control field (16 bit CRC code)
//
// - MASTER_CHANNEL_TM(masterChannelName,
//                     scid,
//                     parentPcid)
//   -- masterChannelName: A name that can be used to uniquely identify this master channel
//   -- parentPcid: Associates this master channel with a specific physical channel
//   -- scid: A 10 bit id assigned by CCSDS, for uniquely defining a master channel
//
// - MASTER_CHANNEL_TC(masterChannelName,
//                     scid,
//                     parentPcid)
//   -- masterChannelName: A name that can be used to uniquely identify this master channel
//   -- scid: A 10 bit id assigned by CCSDS, for uniquely defining a master channel
//   -- parentPcid: Associates this master channel with a specific physical channel
//
// - VIRTUAL_CHANNEL_TM(virtualChannelName,
//                      vcid,
//                      parentScid,
//                      associatedSdlsSPI,
//                      secondaryHeaderPresent,
//                      secondaryHeaderLength,
//                      ocfFieldPresent,
//                      synchronization,
//                      repetitions,
//                      frameCapacity,
//                      packetCapacity)
//   -- virtualChannelName: A name that can be used to uniquely identify this virtual channel
//   -- vcid: A 6 bit id (unique for all TM virtual channels under a specific TM master channel)
//   -- parentScid: Associates this virtual channel with a specific master channel
//   -- associatedSdls: Security parameter index associated with this virtual channel. Unimplemented for TM frames
//                      (unimplemented, this value is ignored)
//   -- secondaryHeaderPresent: Unimplemented (unimplemented, this value is ignored)
//   -- secondaryHeaderLength: Unimplemented (unimplemented, this value is ignored)
//   -- ocfFieldPresent: Whether the frame has an operational control field. In this implementation, the
//                       ocf field carries CLCWs generated by the COP-1 procedures
//   -- synchronization: Use "SynchronizationFlag::OCTET_SYNCHRONIZED_FORWARD_ORDERED" if the frame payload
//                       has a known structure (this version of the protocol supports "Space Packets" and
//                       "Encapsulation Packets"). If the packet has a different structure, enter
//                       "SynchronizationFlag::VCA_SDU"
//   -- repetitions: How many times each frame will be transmitted to the Channel Coding and Synchronization Sublayer
//   -- frameCapacity: Maximum amount of frames this channel can support (affects memory allocation size)
//   -- packetCapacity: Maximum amount of packets this channel can support (affects memory allocation size). A packet
//                      is defined as the data unit carried by the payload field of a frame.
//
// - VIRTUAL_CHANNEL_TC(virtualChannelName,
//                      vcid,
//                      parentScid,
//                      segHeaderPresent,
//                      blocking,
//                      copInEffect,
//                      associatedSdlsSPI,
//                      repetitions,
//                      frameCapacity,
//                      typeAdPacketCapacity,
//                      typeBdPacketCapacity)
//   -- virtualChannelName: A name that can be used to uniquely identify this virtual channel
//   -- vcid: A 6 bit id (unique for all TM virtual channels under a specific TM master channel)
//   -- parentScid: Associates this virtual channel with a specific master channel
//   -- segHeaderPresent: A value of non zero indicates that map channels exist under this virtual channel
//   -- blocking: A value of non zero allows combining multiple small TCs in a single TC transfer frame. Superseded in
//                the scenario that map channels exist under this virtual channel.
//   -- copInEffect: A value of non zero indicates that COP-1 frame acknowledgement system is active for this channel.
//                   For COP-1 to work, ensure that a COP1() object is associated with this channel.
//   -- vcid: A 6 bit id (unique for all TM virtual channels under a specific TM master channel)
//   -- repetitions: How many times each frame will be transmitted to the Channel Coding and Synchronization Sublayer
//   -- associatedSdlsSPI: Security parameter index associated with this virtual channel. Value 0 indicates
//                         that frames in this channel are not encrypted, nor authenticated. Superseded in the scenario
//                         that map channels exist under this virtual channel. Ensure that a SECURITY_ASSOCIATION()
//                         with this associatedSdls exists.
//   -- frameCapacity: Maximum amount of frames this channel can support (affects memory allocation size)
//                     WARNING: If map channels exist under this virtual channel this value MUST be set to 0.
//                              Otherwise, an excess amount of memory will be allocated
//   -- typeAdPacketCapacity, typeBdPacketCapacity: Amount of packets this channel can support (affects memory
//                     allocation size). Packets are defined as the data units carried by the payload field of a frame.
//                     Type AD packets are subject to the COP-1 process, while Type BD are expedited (a similar analogy
//                     with internet protocols is TCP segments vs UDP datagrams). The value typeAdPacketCapacity is
//                     ignored if copInEffect == 0, and type-AD packets will not be accepted by this channel.
//                     WARNING: If map channels exist under this virtual channel those values MUST be set to0.
//                              Otherwise, an excess amount of memory will be allocated.
//
// - MAP_CHANNEL(mapChannelName,
//               mapid,
//               parentVcid,
//               parentScid,
//               blocking,
//               segmentation,
//               associatedSdlsSPI,
//               frameCapacity,
//               typeAdPacketCapacity,
//               typeBdPacketCapacity)
//   -- mapChannelName: A name that can be used to uniquely identify this map channel
//   -- mapid: A 6 bit id (unique for all map channels under a specific TC virtual channel)
//   -- parentVcid: Associates this map with a specific virtual channel
//   -- parentScid: This id is necessary to uniquely identify 2 map channels that have the same parentVcid, meaning
//                  their parent virtual channels belong to different master channels and have the same vcid.
//   -- blocking: A value of non zero allows combining multiple small TCs in a single TC transfer frame
//   -- segmentation: A value of non zero allows splitting large TCs in multiple TC transfer frames
//   -- associatedSdlsSPI: Security parameter index associated with this virtual channel. A value of 0 indicates that
//                         frames in this channel are not encrypted, nor authenticated. Superseded in the scenario
//                         that map channels exist under this virtual channel
//   -- frameCapacity: Maximum amount of frames this channel can support (affects memory allocation size)
//   -- typeAdPacketCapacity, typeBdPacketCapacity: Amount of packets this channel can support (affects memory
//                     allocation size). Packets are defined as the data units carried by the payload field of a frame.
//                     Type AD packets are subject to the COP-1 process, while Type BD are expedited (a similar analogy
//                     with internet protocols is TCP segments vs UDP datagrams). The value typeAdPacketCapacity is
//                     ignored if copInEffect == 0, and type-AD packets will not be accepted by this channel.
//
// - COP1(vcid,
//        tiInitial,
//        transmissionLimit,
//        fopSlidingWindowWidth,
//        timeoutType,
//        farmSlidingWindowWidth,
//        farmPositiveWindowWidth,
//        farmNegativeWindowWidth,
//        clcwReportInterval)
//   -- vcid: A 6 bit that associates this COP1 object with a specific virtual channel
//   -- tiInitial: A reverse countdown timer value in milliseconds. The ground segment will wait for this amount of
//                 time before retransmitting a TC frame
//   -- transmissionLimit: Amount of retransmissions, before the ground segment announces a break in the link
//   -- fopSlidingWindowWidth: Limits the amount of TC frames the ground segment can transmit ahead of the last
//                             acknowledged frame
//   -- timeoutType: Determines type of action when the transmission limit is reached and the timer is expired
//   -- farmSlidingWindowWidth, farmPositiveWindowWidth, farmNegativeWindowWidth: Determine the range of
//      allowed sequence numbers the space segment can accept
//   -- clcwReportInterval: CLCW generation period by the space segment (in milliseconds) CLCWs are carried by TM
//                          frames and are used by the ground segment to assess the status of accepted TCs by the
//                          space segment
//
// - SECURITY_ASSOCIATION(spi,
//                        authenticationAlgorithm,
//                        enryptionAlgorithm,
//                        authKey)
//   -- spi: Security parameter index. Virtual and map channels can be associated with this security association, by
//           using this index
//   -- authenticationAlgorithm: Currently, only "AuthenticationAlgorithm::HMAC_SHA256_40_BIT" is supported. If no
//                               authentication is needed, use "AuthenticationAlgorithm::NO_AUTHENTICATION"
//   -- encryptionAlgorithm: Unimplemented. This value is ignored
//
//   NOTE: When the authentication service is enabled, an authentication key is required. This key should be placed in
//         AuthenticationKey.hpp


PHYSICAL_CHANNEL(TestPhysicalChannel, TransferFrameVersionNumber::TM_TC_SYNCHRONOUS_TRANSFER_FRAME_V1, 1024, 1024, 1, 1, 1000, 1, 1)